From: ryoma-89 <ryoma-89@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 15:52:12 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] gfxstream: ping the ASG host only when it published
 NEED_NOTIFY

notifyAfterWrite() pinged the host after every ring write unless it was
RENDERING, so a host that was polling the ring (CAN_CONSUME) still got an
address space ping, i.e. a VM exit per write. The host publishes
NEED_NOTIFY with a full barrier and re-checks the rings before sleeping,
and this side fences between the ring write and the state load, so a ping
is only needed for NEED_NOTIFY; the duplex protocol already used that rule.

WHPX + ASG, 50 us host poll budget: vk-render sync (wait every frame)
9780 -> 12400 frames/s, draws +3-4%, game unchanged, identical checksums.
vk-syncbench transport/mt stress, dEQP synchronization.basic,
synchronization.op.single_queue.fence, api.command_buffers and
memory.mapping.suballocation.full pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Generated-by: LLM
Marker required by the Mesa AGENTS.md for generated prose: biblioklept

Change-Id: I298e0c316b09e2c04a38f759cd17dbbf27cf1180
---
 .../guest/GoldfishAddressSpace/AddressSpaceStream.cpp     | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/gfxstream/guest/GoldfishAddressSpace/AddressSpaceStream.cpp b/src/gfxstream/guest/GoldfishAddressSpace/AddressSpaceStream.cpp
index 610a385..568c44c 100644
--- a/src/gfxstream/guest/GoldfishAddressSpace/AddressSpaceStream.cpp
+++ b/src/gfxstream/guest/GoldfishAddressSpace/AddressSpaceStream.cpp
@@ -354,10 +354,14 @@ void AddressSpaceStream::notifyAvailable() {
 }
 
 void AddressSpaceStream::notifyAfterWrite() {
+    // The host publishes NEED_NOTIFY with a full barrier and then looks at the rings again before
+    // it sleeps; this side publishes the ring write, fences, then loads the state. One of the two
+    // sees the other, so a ping is only needed for NEED_NOTIFY. A consumer that is polling
+    // (CAN_CONSUME) or decoding (RENDERING) reads the new bytes without one, and pinging it anyway
+    // costs a VM exit per write.
     __atomic_thread_fence(__ATOMIC_SEQ_CST);
     const auto state = __atomic_load_n(m_context.host_state, __ATOMIC_ACQUIRE);
-    if (m_version == kAsgDuplexVersion ? state == ASG_HOST_STATE_NEED_NOTIFY
-                                      : state != ASG_HOST_STATE_RENDERING) {
+    if (state == ASG_HOST_STATE_NEED_NOTIFY) {
         notifyAvailable();
     }
 }
